<main id="main">

<section class="bk-hero"><div class="bk-hero-i pxw"><img data-px=".16" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1786025083224-220e39cb1e22?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&h=1200&q=75" alt="a green canvas backpack with leather straps and buckles on a yellow chair" width="1800" height="1200" fetchpriority="high"></div><div class="bk-hero-t"><p class="bk-ey">The art of the fastening</p><h1 aria-label="Buckled"><span>B</span><span>u</span><span>c</span><span>k</span><span>l</span><span>e</span><span>d</span></h1><p class="bk-hero-l">An independent guide to bags that close with a buckle: the hardware, the leather and the craft behind them.</p></div><div class="bk-hero-b"><span>Scroll to discover</span><i></i></div></section>

<section class="bk-s"><div class="bk-w bk-in"><p class="bk-big rv">A buckle is the oldest, simplest way to close a bag. It is also the most <em>honest</em>: every part is visible, and every part can be repaired.</p><div class="bk-in-n stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="5">5</b><span>parts in every buckle</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="4">4</b><span>common hardware metals</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="20">20</b><span>years a good bag can last</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s bk-dk" id="anatomy"><div class="bk-w bk-an"><div class="bk-an-i"><div class="bk-an-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590324099257-2a4acb01b0b1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=760&q=75" alt="a black leather belt with a silver buckle" width="760" height="760" loading="lazy"><button class="bk-dot" style="left:28%;top:48%" data-p="0" aria-label="Frame">1</button><button class="bk-dot" style="left:52%;top:40%" data-p="1" aria-label="Prong">2</button><button class="bk-dot" style="left:44%;top:66%" data-p="2" aria-label="Keeper">3</button><button class="bk-dot" style="left:74%;top:56%" data-p="3" aria-label="Holes">4</button><button class="bk-dot" style="left:14%;top:30%" data-p="4" aria-label="Chape">5</button></div></div><div><p class="bk-ey">Buckle anatomy</p><h2 class="rv">Five parts, perfectly simple</h2><div class="bk-part" id="an-o" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="bk-an-nav" id="an-n"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s bk-sto"><div class="bk-w bk-sto-h"><div><p class="bk-ey">From hide to bag</p><h2 class="rv">The making, in four chapters</h2></div><p class="bk-hint">Drag</p></div><div class="hs bk-hs"><div class="bk-st"><div class="bk-st-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794429967137-c326943dc721?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="workers processing leather in round stone vats at a tannery" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><span>I</span><h3>The tannery</h3><p>Hides are cleaned and tanned until they become supple, lasting leather.</p></div><div class="bk-st"><div class="bk-st-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794093439194-48b177774edb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="a dark archway opening onto a sunlit courtyard hung with leather hides" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><span>II</span><h3>The drying</h3><p>Tanned hides dry slowly in the open air, keeping their character.</p></div><div class="bk-st"><div class="bk-st-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1778882999785-9e75a2207d0c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="close-up of textured brown leather" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><span>III</span><h3>The grain</h3><p>Full-grain leather keeps its natural surface, and ages with you.</p></div><div class="bk-st"><div class="bk-st-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1790253719855-e6f58150fc7f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=720&q=75" alt="a cluttered workbench in a repair shop with tools and bags" width="560" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><span>IV</span><h3>The bench</h3><p>Straps are cut, edges finished and buckles fixed by hand.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s" id="styles"><div class="bk-w"><div class="bk-cen"><p class="bk-ey">The buckle library</p><h2 class="rv">Five fastenings to know</h2></div><div class="bk-lib rv"><div class="bk-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Buckle types"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-s="0">Tongue</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="1">Turn-lock</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="2">Push-lock</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="3">Slide</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-s="4">Hidden magnet</button></div><div class="bk-lib-g"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 200" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="30" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="#2A1E15"/><path id="ls-f" d="" fill="#9A5B2E"/><g id="ls-h"></g></svg><div id="ls-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s bk-dk" id="strap"><div class="bk-w bk-sf"><div><p class="bk-ey">Strap fitter</p><h2 class="rv">Find your hole</h2><p class="bk-p">Shoulder, crossbody or hand: the right strap length puts the bag where you reach for it. Tell us your height and how you carry.</p><label for="sf-h" class="bk-lab">Your height <output id="sf-hv">170 cm</output><input type="range" id="sf-h" min="145" max="200" value="170"></label><div class="bk-carry" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Carry style"><label><input type="radio" name="cs" value="0" checked><span>Shoulder</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="cs" value="1"><span>Crossbody</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="cs" value="2"><span>Short handle</span></label></div><div class="bk-sf-o" id="sf-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div><div class="bk-strap"><svg viewBox="0 0 520 120" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="10" y="44" width="500" height="32" rx="6" fill="#9A5B2E"/><g id="sf-holes"></g><rect x="14" y="36" width="44" height="48" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="#C9A46A" stroke-width="5"/><line x1="36" y1="40" x2="36" y2="80" stroke="#C9A46A" stroke-width="4"/></svg><p class="bk-small">Each hole is usually 2&ndash;2.5 cm apart. The middle hole gives you room either way.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s"><div class="bk-w"><div class="bk-cen"><p class="bk-ey">The collection</p><h2 class="rv">Shapes worth owning</h2></div><div class="bk-col stg"><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1622560480605-d83c853bc5c3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=560&q=75" alt="a brown leather backpack on a white surface" width="440" height="560" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The leather backpack</b><span>Two buckled straps, hands free</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1783224441937-bea6ee7d0aa5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=560&q=75" alt="a person in a green shirt carrying a pink shoulder bag" width="440" height="560" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The shoulder bag</b><span>One buckle, softly structured</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1549943872-f7ff0b2b51be?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=560&q=75" alt="a brown and black leather backpack on the ground" width="440" height="560" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The weekend pack</b><span>Buckles that take a load</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-s bk-care"><div class="bk-w bk-ca"><div><p class="bk-ey">Hardware care</p><h2 class="rv">Choose your metal</h2><div class="bk-metal" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Hardware metal"><label><input type="radio" name="mt" value="0" checked><span style="--m:linear-gradient(135deg,#E2C27A,#A07B3B)">Solid brass</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="mt" value="1"><span style="--m:linear-gradient(135deg,#F0F0EE,#9A9C9F)">Nickel or steel</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="mt" value="2"><span style="--m:linear-gradient(135deg,#F3D99B,#C69A45)">Gold-tone plated</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="mt" value="3"><span style="--m:linear-gradient(135deg,#5B5A58,#1E1D1C)">Gunmetal or black</span></label></div></div><div class="bk-ca-o" id="mt-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></section>

<section class="bk-gl"><a href="buckle-bag-guide.html" class="bk-gl-a"><div class="bk-gl-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503956011720-b85f3dcf88ce?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=600&q=75" alt="a black rucksack in shallow focus" width="900" height="600" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bk-gl-t"><span>Chapter I</span><b>Choosing a Buckle Bag</b><em>Leather, hardware, stitching and strap, and what to check before you buy.</em><i>Read &rarr;</i></div></a><a href="bag-hardware-care-guide.html" class="bk-gl-a"><div class="bk-gl-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1789845137118-fa4566647ee4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=600&q=75" alt="a golden leather cuff with folded pleats in warm light" width="900" height="600" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bk-gl-t"><span>Chapter II</span><b>Hardware Care</b><em>Cleaning, polishing and protecting buckles, rings and clasps.</em><i>Read &rarr;</i></div></a></section>

